WEBVTT

00:01.660 --> 00:04.030
Narrator: Previously
on "Final Space"...

00:04.070 --> 00:05.900
After five years of jail time
alone on a prison ship,

00:05.930 --> 00:09.170
our hero Gary made not one,
but two friends.

00:09.210 --> 00:12.240
One is a planet-killer, the
other a deadly bounty hunter.

00:12.280 --> 00:14.880
And both of them lead right
back to the Lord Commander,

00:14.910 --> 00:17.010
who's kind of a jerk-face.
Well, guess what?!

00:17.050 --> 00:19.820
We're off to a great start,
so buckle up those butt cheeks,

00:19.850 --> 00:22.590
'cause things are
about to get heavy.

00:25.890 --> 00:30.230
H.U.E.: Gary, you have eight
minutes of oxygen left.

00:30.260 --> 00:32.730
H.U.E., if you had
eight minutes to live

00:32.760 --> 00:35.730
and you could do anything
you wanted, what would you do?

00:35.760 --> 00:38.200
Facticulating.
Ahh.

00:38.230 --> 00:41.670
I would transfer my A.I.
into a corporeal being

00:41.700 --> 00:44.770
and go see Paris.

00:44.810 --> 00:49.510
Oh, that's lame!
I mean, wow. Super...cool.

00:49.550 --> 00:51.550
What would you do,
Gary?

00:51.580 --> 00:53.050
Absolutely anything.

00:53.080 --> 00:55.250
And I mean anything with Quinn.

00:55.280 --> 00:57.920
I mean, we could watch
"Space Drive" for all I care.

00:57.950 --> 01:01.620
I'm sorry things
turned out this way.

01:01.660 --> 01:03.060
Crap happens.

01:03.090 --> 01:12.940
♪♪

01:12.970 --> 01:23.280
♪♪

01:23.310 --> 01:31.120
♪♪

01:31.150 --> 01:38.560
♪♪

01:38.590 --> 01:41.630
KVN: ♪ Holes, holes, holes,
holes, cover up these holes ♪

01:41.660 --> 01:43.130
♪ Plug these holes

01:43.170 --> 01:44.800
♪ Holes, holes, holes, holes

01:44.830 --> 01:46.400
♪ Nothing but holes,
nothing but holes ♪

01:46.440 --> 01:49.100
♪ Nothing but holes,
but holes, but holes ♪

01:49.140 --> 01:51.140
♪ Holes, holes, holes, holes,
cover up these holes ♪

01:51.170 --> 01:52.740
♪ Plug these holes,
holes, holes ♪

01:52.780 --> 01:53.980
♪ Nothing but holes

01:54.010 --> 01:55.240
♪ Holes, holes, holes

01:55.280 --> 01:56.450
♪ But holes

01:56.480 --> 01:57.780
♪ Plug these -- plug

01:57.810 --> 01:59.780
♪ Plug these holes,
holes ♪

01:59.820 --> 02:02.820
♪ Holes, holes, holes, holes

02:02.850 --> 02:06.160
Quinn, it's me, Gary. Things
have been great on my end.

02:06.190 --> 02:08.660
I made what I believe to be
a potential new friend.

02:08.690 --> 02:10.160
Yes, he boarded
the ship to kill me

02:10.190 --> 02:11.660
and take my little
green ball friend,

02:11.690 --> 02:16.530
but Avocato is one
great card player.

02:16.570 --> 02:18.870
Any more cards and I
will shoot myself.

02:18.900 --> 02:21.340
I'm gonna shoot you
if you don't play cards.

02:21.370 --> 02:23.670
-I'll let you shoot me.
-Um, oh -- real--

02:23.710 --> 02:25.310
Well, then I'm gonna
shoot myself!

02:25.340 --> 02:26.540
What? Why?

02:26.580 --> 02:28.340
Frickin' figure it out.
Figure it out.

02:28.380 --> 02:31.350
And our newest member
is this little guy!

02:31.380 --> 02:32.520
His name's Mooncake.

02:32.550 --> 02:33.520
Ooh!

02:33.550 --> 02:35.020
Everyone loves him.

02:35.050 --> 02:36.650
That little
green snot-ball

02:36.690 --> 02:38.550
is a planet-destroying
super-weapon

02:38.590 --> 02:39.860
that's gonna
get us killed.

02:39.890 --> 02:43.530
You, sir, just stepped
over the line.

02:43.560 --> 02:45.030
Mooncake has feelings.

02:45.060 --> 02:47.500
And you just peed all over them
with your cat whiz.

02:47.530 --> 02:50.870
Gary: Yep. Things have been
going pretty great.

02:50.900 --> 02:52.340
Get back to me.
No rush.

02:52.370 --> 02:54.540
It's just I haven't talked
to a human lady person

02:54.570 --> 02:57.370
in, like, five years.

02:57.410 --> 03:00.710
Well, yours forever.
Thunder bandit!

03:00.740 --> 03:01.810
Message sent.

03:01.840 --> 03:03.580
I crushed it...again!

03:03.610 --> 03:05.380
[ Breathes deeply ]

03:05.410 --> 03:06.650
[ Device beeps ]

03:06.680 --> 03:07.650
Quinn.

03:07.680 --> 03:09.220
Hey, Quinn,
it's Tribor.

03:09.250 --> 03:11.320
An Infinity Guard ship
has crashed.

03:11.350 --> 03:13.760
How did it crash,
we don't know.

03:13.790 --> 03:15.560
We need you on the scene.

03:15.590 --> 03:17.490
On my way.

03:17.530 --> 03:20.430
Ha. Oh, mama. Oh, boy.

03:20.460 --> 03:21.730
Oh!

03:21.760 --> 03:23.770
H.U.E.:
Unauthorized scan detected.

03:23.800 --> 03:26.200
[ Alarm blaring ]

03:26.240 --> 03:27.270
What ya doing, Gary?

03:29.610 --> 03:32.940
Gotcha.
Lord Commander -- agh!

03:32.980 --> 03:34.080
Hmm.

03:34.110 --> 03:36.950
Set course
for Tera Con Prime.

03:41.950 --> 03:43.090
[ Electricity crackling ]

03:43.120 --> 03:44.620
What the heck
is this thing?

03:44.650 --> 03:47.220
A Ventrexian
stealth probe -- Turk.

03:47.260 --> 03:48.760
Of course, Turk.

03:48.790 --> 03:49.960
Who the hell is Turk?

03:49.990 --> 03:51.760
A bounty hunter --
like me.

03:51.790 --> 03:53.360
If he scanned Mooncake,

03:53.400 --> 03:55.530
he'll be on his way back
to the Lord Commander

03:55.560 --> 03:57.100
to gather reinforcements.
-Mm-hmm.

03:57.130 --> 03:58.870
-Unless we stop him first.
-Mm-hmm.

03:58.900 --> 04:01.200
It we don't, they will
capture Mooncake.

04:01.240 --> 04:02.770
-Mnh-mnh.
-And take us to the Dark Zone.

04:02.810 --> 04:04.770
Mnh-mnh.
And torture us
with zargon slugs.

04:04.810 --> 04:06.310
Mnh-mnh.

04:06.340 --> 04:09.280
Or we're gonna suffer pain
and anguish for eternity.

04:09.310 --> 04:11.450
Oh.
And the only way
to stop them is with salt.

04:11.480 --> 04:15.280
Oh.
And there's no salt
in the Dark Zone.

04:15.320 --> 04:16.490
Hmm.

04:16.520 --> 04:20.890
Sounds like I got these
buttery buns into a hot vise.

04:20.920 --> 04:23.060
How do I stop them?
-You don't.

04:23.090 --> 04:24.660
But together,
we've got a shot.

04:24.690 --> 04:27.130
Get me out of these cuffs,
and we'll go after him.

04:27.160 --> 04:29.260
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, cowboy!

04:29.300 --> 04:30.400
You tried to kill me.

04:30.430 --> 04:33.670
If you want me to trust you,
first we clasp.

04:33.700 --> 04:34.970
I'm not doing that.

04:35.000 --> 04:37.140
Oh, yes, you will.
You will do that.

04:37.170 --> 04:39.310
We've enjoyed recreational
cards together.

04:39.340 --> 04:40.810
This is the next step.

04:40.840 --> 04:42.650
A hand-to-hand bond
that forges

04:42.680 --> 04:45.280
the completion
of a newfound trust.

04:45.310 --> 04:47.850
We don't have to get balls
to the wind naked, do we?

04:47.880 --> 04:51.020
Tradition demands yes.
But you're lucky.

04:51.050 --> 04:53.020
I'm more of a progressive.

04:53.060 --> 04:55.920
Trust mode engaged.

04:55.960 --> 04:58.130
It's been five years
since I've been off this ship!

04:58.160 --> 05:02.000
I am pumped for adventure!
Let's get this guy!

05:02.030 --> 05:03.270
H.U.E., open the airlock.

05:03.300 --> 05:05.000
H.U.E.:
You are a prisoner.

05:05.030 --> 05:06.770
How will I know
you won't run?

05:06.800 --> 05:07.840
-I got nowhere to g--
-Inject.

05:07.870 --> 05:09.200
Ow!
What the freak was that?!

05:09.240 --> 05:12.010
If you are not back aboard
this ship in five hours,

05:12.040 --> 05:14.480
your brain will go
into convulsive spasms

05:14.510 --> 05:16.350
and then explode.

05:16.380 --> 05:18.180
Let's go!

05:18.210 --> 05:19.520
Shouldn't we take Mooncake?

05:19.550 --> 05:22.150
It's too dangerous.
Make haste, make haste!

05:22.180 --> 05:23.350
I'll miss you, bud.
Be good.

05:23.390 --> 05:25.650
And don't whiz on
any of my stuff.

05:25.690 --> 05:31.860
♪♪

05:31.890 --> 05:38.170
♪♪

05:38.200 --> 05:40.540
Oh, oh!
Street meat!

05:40.570 --> 05:42.140
They got street meat, Avocato!

05:42.170 --> 05:43.870
-Focus.
-Okay, I'm focused.

05:43.910 --> 05:46.210
Gary: All right,
we're getting Turk.

05:49.380 --> 05:54.520
For the galaxy, for eternity,
for Lord Commander.

05:57.220 --> 05:58.750
You're lucky that we
even made it here.

05:58.790 --> 06:00.720
They don't take kindly
to Homo sapiens.

06:00.760 --> 06:01.990
Now let's go to tier 24

06:02.020 --> 06:03.990
and get you
identification papers.

06:04.030 --> 06:06.430
-Ha! I don't need papers.
-Or they'll liquify you.

06:06.460 --> 06:09.400
Did you just say liquify?
Or was that a brain spasm?

06:09.430 --> 06:12.100
Is it happening?
Oh, my crap, it's happening.

06:12.130 --> 06:15.900
Or we'll kill you.

06:15.940 --> 06:17.240
Gary, stay close.

06:17.270 --> 06:20.080
Right, don't worry.
I'm not going anywhere.

06:20.110 --> 06:22.380
-Gary!
-Getting some street meat!

06:22.410 --> 06:25.580
Identification papers!

06:25.610 --> 06:28.780
Um, I must have
left them in, um...

06:28.820 --> 06:31.450
We got a runner.

06:33.460 --> 06:36.390
Maybe we should
get some papers.

06:36.430 --> 06:37.360
Mm-hmm.

06:37.390 --> 06:40.760
KVN: Welcome
to the hangar bay!

06:40.800 --> 06:42.130
But I call it
the tiger's nest.

06:42.160 --> 06:43.700
And I bet
you're wondering why.

06:43.730 --> 06:45.430
Well, okay,
I'll tell you.

06:45.470 --> 06:46.870
Whoo!

06:46.900 --> 06:48.440
Uh, excuse me,
can I help you?

06:48.470 --> 06:52.440
Uh, hello.
Run away! Run away!

06:59.480 --> 07:03.220
Ahh. Avocato,
it's so good to see you.

07:03.250 --> 07:06.620
What brings you to my
little shop of doo-dads?

07:06.660 --> 07:07.760
Cut the crap, Clarence!

07:07.790 --> 07:09.630
Yeah,
cut the crap, Clarence.

07:09.660 --> 07:11.630
-We need papers.
-That's right, papers.

07:11.660 --> 07:14.460
Well,
papers are not cheap.

07:14.500 --> 07:15.800
-[ Growls ]
-Oh!

07:15.830 --> 07:17.970
Neither is your life,
and I saved that.

07:18.000 --> 07:19.640
Yes, right,
I suppose you did.

07:19.670 --> 07:22.910
But this is the last time.
Your papers are easy.

07:22.940 --> 07:24.810
But this primate...
-Hey!

07:24.840 --> 07:26.340
...is gonna be much
more difficult.

07:26.370 --> 07:30.250
Get your finger
out of my tummy.

07:30.280 --> 07:32.480
Ooh! It speaks.

07:32.520 --> 07:34.350
I guess you can
train anything.

07:34.380 --> 07:37.290
I'll touch you any time
I wish, primate!

07:37.320 --> 07:38.620
Hmm.

07:38.650 --> 07:41.320
Yes, no, not that one.
Hold on a second.

07:41.360 --> 07:42.690
Down here at the bottom,
possibly.

07:42.730 --> 07:45.090
Oh, yes, here we go.

07:45.130 --> 07:46.600
Skin of a dead Hooblat.

07:46.630 --> 07:48.660
I have to get
in this thing?

07:48.700 --> 07:51.470
It's like a slippery
pita pocket.

07:51.500 --> 07:53.340
You want to be liquefied
and have Mooncake

07:53.370 --> 07:54.670
and the Galaxy 1 destroyed?

07:54.700 --> 07:57.010
No, h-- How the hell
do you know that?

07:57.040 --> 08:00.140
It's everywhere.
It's all anyone's talking about.

08:00.180 --> 08:01.280
Huh.

08:01.310 --> 08:03.150
Both: Get in the skin!

08:03.180 --> 08:04.680
For Mooncake.

08:04.710 --> 08:07.380
Oh, my God,
it's so warm!

08:07.420 --> 08:09.690
Oh, it's -- and wet!
Oh.

08:09.720 --> 08:12.520
It actually kind of
feels kind of nice,

08:12.560 --> 08:15.190
like a pair of warm,
wet house slippers.

08:19.190 --> 08:20.530
It doesn't make any sense.

08:20.560 --> 08:23.200
I know. It doesn't
make any sense.

08:23.230 --> 08:24.570
I wish there was sense.

08:24.600 --> 08:26.400
Where did
all the sense go?

08:26.430 --> 08:28.700
I don't get it.
It's an Imperium T3.

08:28.740 --> 08:30.640
These things don't crash.

08:30.670 --> 08:32.980
They don't crash,
you're right.

08:33.010 --> 08:34.710
It doesn't
make any sense.

08:34.740 --> 08:35.980
Why would it crash?

08:36.010 --> 08:38.810
Tribor,
look me in the eye.

08:38.850 --> 08:40.980
Now shut up.
-I should shut up.

08:41.020 --> 08:43.550
Why do I keep talking?
-Are you reading this?

08:43.590 --> 08:45.350
The gravitational
constant is shifting.

08:45.390 --> 08:47.560
I am seeing it.
I am!

08:47.590 --> 08:49.020
A disturbance this strong

08:49.060 --> 08:52.330
can literally tear
the universe apart.

08:52.360 --> 08:53.730
H.U.E.: Intruder alert.

08:53.760 --> 08:56.930
Initiating anti-gravity
countermeasures.

08:56.970 --> 09:03.110
♪♪

09:03.140 --> 09:06.440
Sames, initiate
defense sequence.

09:06.470 --> 09:12.080
♪♪

09:12.110 --> 09:15.850
Anyway, I'm kind of in charge
of security around here,

09:15.880 --> 09:18.050
which brings me
to a big ask.

09:18.090 --> 09:20.220
Could you go out there
and get me a cookie?

09:20.260 --> 09:22.020
-Chocli.
-Score!

09:22.060 --> 09:24.630
All right, I'll stay here
and guard the fort.

09:27.430 --> 09:28.800
How do I look?
Be honest.

09:28.830 --> 09:30.600
-I'd give you a 2.
-Just a 2?

09:30.630 --> 09:32.130
Get my hair done
or something, you know.

09:32.170 --> 09:33.240
How about no?

09:33.270 --> 09:34.600
No, seriously,
I could get highlights.

09:34.640 --> 09:36.100
I could get ombre hair,
you know?

09:36.140 --> 09:37.270
I can't believe it.

09:37.310 --> 09:39.140
Believe it, because this
ombre hair is happening.

09:39.170 --> 09:41.780
-No. Turk!
-Oh, crap, it is Turk.

09:41.810 --> 09:43.710
What are you looking at?
What are you looking at?

09:43.750 --> 09:46.110
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

09:46.150 --> 09:47.120
Hmm.

09:47.150 --> 09:49.950
[ Choking ]

09:49.990 --> 09:51.250
Thought you could
rat us out, huh?

09:51.290 --> 09:54.890
How the hell are you,
you old bag?

09:54.920 --> 09:58.590
Okay.
That just hurts.

09:58.630 --> 09:59.900
Avocato!

09:59.930 --> 10:01.300
No!

10:01.330 --> 10:02.930
Give me one reason
I don't kill you right now

10:02.970 --> 10:04.570
for leaving me to die
on that ship!

10:04.600 --> 10:07.140
Because I know
where your son is.

10:07.170 --> 10:10.240
My son?
Where? Where is he?

10:10.270 --> 10:12.570
Holding cell 43.

10:12.610 --> 10:14.740
He's...he's here?

10:14.780 --> 10:16.580
Now let me go.

10:16.610 --> 10:18.810
I'll let you go.

10:18.850 --> 10:20.650
I'll let you go
to Hell.

10:20.680 --> 10:29.790
[ Screaming ]

10:29.830 --> 10:30.960
[ Screaming stops ]

10:30.990 --> 10:36.500
[ Screaming resumes ]

10:36.530 --> 10:38.830
I'm coming, Avocato.

10:41.540 --> 10:43.840
Melanie Duinger, level 4.

10:43.870 --> 10:45.540
Melanie Du--
what -- what?!

10:45.570 --> 10:47.680
Aah! Oh!

10:47.710 --> 10:49.950
-Mommy!
-Mommy!

10:49.980 --> 10:53.450
-You're back!
-I sure am!

10:53.480 --> 10:55.480
Oh, no!
-Melanie!

10:55.520 --> 10:59.890
Oh, they told us
you were dead!

10:59.920 --> 11:01.060
Oh!

11:01.090 --> 11:05.330
Everything with
your sister was a mistake.

11:05.360 --> 11:08.700
Oh, my crap.

11:23.410 --> 11:25.480
Sit tight.

11:25.510 --> 11:26.720
I can't hear you.

11:26.750 --> 11:28.850
I messed up.
I messed up bad!

11:28.880 --> 11:30.890
But I'm not gonna
leave you here. I promise.

11:30.920 --> 11:33.160
I'll do
whatever it takes.

11:33.190 --> 11:37.260
No, Dad! Dad, run!
It's a trap!

11:37.290 --> 11:40.730
Dad, watch out!

11:40.760 --> 11:43.900
Dad, Dad, Dad, no!

11:43.930 --> 11:46.770
Take him
to the Lord Commander.

11:49.440 --> 11:50.910
I love Mommy more!

11:50.940 --> 11:53.280
No, I love Mommy more!

11:53.310 --> 11:54.740
Okay, just, uh -- stop --

11:54.780 --> 11:57.280
keep -- stop tugging
too hard, babies.

11:57.310 --> 11:59.550
[ All scream ]

11:59.580 --> 12:02.280
Melanie?!
Oh, God!

12:04.050 --> 12:07.060
So you probably have
a few questions.

12:07.090 --> 12:09.860
Get out of here,
you maniac!

12:09.890 --> 12:12.390
[ All crying ]

12:12.430 --> 12:13.830
Hyah!

12:15.660 --> 12:17.270
Huh!

12:20.640 --> 12:22.100
Avocato!

12:23.270 --> 12:24.810
Whew.

12:24.840 --> 12:26.940
The clasp of friends.

12:28.640 --> 12:31.380
Only two hours till my brain
shoots out of my eyes.

12:31.410 --> 12:32.750
I gotta move fast.

12:35.650 --> 12:38.450
[ Indistinct conversations ]

12:38.490 --> 12:39.960
Sir,
there's an emergency.

12:39.990 --> 12:42.660
We need to ground all Infinity
Guard cruisers immediately.

12:42.690 --> 12:44.090
What?!
Not again, Quinn.

12:44.130 --> 12:46.090
There's a cosmic
disaster taking place.

12:46.130 --> 12:47.760
We need to find out
what's causing --

12:47.800 --> 12:49.230
Quinn, shut up!

12:49.260 --> 12:51.330
The Imperium T3 crashed
because of human error.

12:51.370 --> 12:55.140
Yeah? Tell that to science.
You're an idiot.

12:55.170 --> 12:57.810
-Back me up, Captain.
-Time to leave, Quinn.

12:57.840 --> 13:00.580
Okay. The Captain
is also an idiot.

13:00.610 --> 13:02.110
Lieutenant?

13:02.140 --> 13:03.310
[ Clicking ]

13:03.350 --> 13:05.450
You're all idiots!
Idiots, idiots!

13:05.480 --> 13:08.150
Are you idiots?
Why would you all be idiots?

13:08.180 --> 13:10.250
I think
you're all very smart.

13:10.290 --> 13:11.020
[ Yelling ]

13:11.050 --> 13:12.620
Well, I gotta go.

13:12.650 --> 13:16.160
H.U.E.: Stop! Stop,
or I will be forced to...

13:20.360 --> 13:25.000
Manual override of AI.
H.U.E. disable...

13:26.840 --> 13:31.940
♪♪

13:31.970 --> 13:33.210
Avocato.

13:33.240 --> 13:34.710
We had a deal.

13:34.740 --> 13:37.780
You promised me E-351

13:37.810 --> 13:41.850
and you failed...
again.

13:41.880 --> 13:44.150
Trust me,
I can do this.

13:44.190 --> 13:45.490
I'm close.

13:45.520 --> 13:49.690
Ooh! Ooh, hurray.
When will it be mine?

13:49.720 --> 13:52.390
Wait, are you hiding it on you?
Is this a game?

13:52.430 --> 13:55.560
I love games.
-I don't have it.

13:55.600 --> 13:58.170
But I can get you
the man who does.

13:58.200 --> 13:59.700
His name is Gary.

13:59.730 --> 14:03.410
I get you him,
you give me back my son.

14:03.440 --> 14:06.070
No deal.

14:06.110 --> 14:08.040
There you are!

14:08.080 --> 14:09.380
What a day I've had, man.

14:09.410 --> 14:11.350
I think I destroyed
a family.

14:11.380 --> 14:14.520
Oh. So how about
we get out of here?

14:14.550 --> 14:18.250
You must be the Gary.

14:18.290 --> 14:20.260
Okay.
Actually, it's just Gary.

14:20.290 --> 14:21.890
-The Gary.
-Just Gary.

14:21.920 --> 14:23.730
You know, just --
just -- there's no...

14:23.760 --> 14:27.030
Where's this "the"
coming from?

14:27.060 --> 14:30.670
Well, this has been great.
But, Avocato, run!

14:30.700 --> 14:34.070
I haven't
introduced myself.

14:34.100 --> 14:37.740
I am the Lord Commander.

14:37.770 --> 14:40.210
Oh, is that you?
That's fantastic.

14:40.240 --> 14:41.880
But we really gotta -- Avocato!

14:41.910 --> 14:47.250
You have something of mine,
and I want it.

14:47.280 --> 14:49.580
Come here, the Gary.

14:49.620 --> 14:52.520
What is going on?
Oh, God!

14:52.550 --> 14:54.520
Okay, this is --
it's nice to be wanted.

14:54.560 --> 14:56.790
But this is --
this is too much want.

14:56.820 --> 15:00.800
Are you going to
give me E-351,

15:00.830 --> 15:04.400
or should I tear you
limb from limb?

15:04.430 --> 15:06.400
Avocato, a little help.

15:06.430 --> 15:08.400
Oh! Oh!

15:08.440 --> 15:11.270
[ Groaning ]

15:11.310 --> 15:13.440
Avocato,
the clasp of friends!

15:13.480 --> 15:15.580
Please, man! Avocato!

15:15.610 --> 15:17.210
[ Sighs ]

15:17.250 --> 15:18.980
[ Groaning ]

15:21.480 --> 15:23.490
Friend mode!
Engaged!

15:23.520 --> 15:24.890
Friend?

15:24.920 --> 15:27.490
He was just
betraying you.

15:27.520 --> 15:30.630
Untrue. We clasped hands.
Right, bro?

15:30.660 --> 15:34.560
I was desperate, man.
I was trying to save my son.

15:34.600 --> 15:37.270
Aah! Oh, my God!

15:39.870 --> 15:42.740
You idiot!
That's my freakin' arm!

15:42.770 --> 15:44.410
You just ripped the thing off!

15:44.440 --> 15:45.840
Aah!

15:45.870 --> 15:49.310
Oh, my God!
Oh, what the freak?!

15:49.340 --> 15:51.710
I'm spraying all my blood!

15:54.780 --> 15:57.690
I am going to murder
your face off!

15:57.720 --> 16:00.320
I will murder
your face on!

16:00.360 --> 16:02.420
That doesn't make
any sense!

16:02.460 --> 16:03.430
-Run!
-Oh!

16:03.460 --> 16:05.160
Come on!

16:05.190 --> 16:07.200
After them!

16:07.230 --> 16:09.460
-Oh, there's so many stairs!
-Quit talking, you idiot!

16:09.500 --> 16:11.500
Why are there
so many stairs?!

16:13.370 --> 16:16.770
Gary,
I can't leave my son.

16:16.800 --> 16:18.010
Oh, we're going,
all right --

16:18.040 --> 16:21.140
and fast -- before
my brain explodes!

16:21.180 --> 16:24.050
[ Gunfire ]

16:24.080 --> 16:25.850
We're not gonna make it
back to the transporter.

16:25.880 --> 16:28.880
Looks like
we got a new ride.

16:28.920 --> 16:32.320
Okay, not ideal,
but still a ride.

16:32.350 --> 16:33.890
Oh, come on!

16:34.490 --> 16:37.360
I don't even know
what that is.

16:37.390 --> 16:40.030
Crap it hard!

16:42.230 --> 16:44.170
We jump to the catwalk.
-Are you insane?

16:44.200 --> 16:47.570
No, I'm super insane.
Ha ha ha!

16:47.600 --> 16:52.740
[ Both screaming ]

16:59.350 --> 17:00.850
Attaboys.

17:00.880 --> 17:02.680
I'll need that suit back.

17:02.720 --> 17:05.250
We're falling!
Oh, my gosh!

17:05.290 --> 17:08.060
Wahhh!

17:08.090 --> 17:11.230
Oh, my God, David, kids!
It's me, your mother!

17:11.260 --> 17:12.990
[ All scream ]

17:13.030 --> 17:15.830
No, my arm!

17:15.860 --> 17:17.930
I forgot my arm
back up there!

17:19.970 --> 17:23.210
This is no good!
H.U.E., pick up, pick up!

17:25.810 --> 17:26.770
Are those what I think
they are?

17:26.810 --> 17:28.010
Viper turrets.

17:28.040 --> 17:29.880
Okay, that's not good.
That's not good!

17:31.050 --> 17:32.910
Quick, hug me.
-Hug you?

17:32.950 --> 17:34.380
-Hug a friend!
-What?!

17:34.420 --> 17:35.620
Hug me!

17:35.650 --> 17:38.720
Oh, we're hugging!

17:41.390 --> 17:45.990
H.U.E.?
H.U.E., come in!

17:48.400 --> 17:49.360
Quinn.

17:49.400 --> 17:50.700
Quinn,
where are you going?

17:50.730 --> 17:52.030
To the first Hawk
I can jack.

17:52.070 --> 17:53.440
Something
big is happening,

17:53.470 --> 17:55.440
and I'm not waiting
while command sits around,

17:55.470 --> 17:56.940
twiddling their wieners.

17:56.970 --> 17:58.240
Maybe I can't stop it,

17:58.270 --> 17:59.570
but I'm going to find out
what it is.

17:59.610 --> 18:01.110
Cover for me.

18:01.140 --> 18:07.750
♪♪

18:07.780 --> 18:10.550
Why would they be
twiddling their wieners?

18:10.590 --> 18:12.650
Why?

18:12.690 --> 18:14.660
Wait, I'm gonna
need six cookies.

18:14.690 --> 18:16.620
And another one.
So seven -- eight cookies.

18:16.660 --> 18:18.230
Wait, nine cookies!

18:18.260 --> 18:21.900
Ah, I guess I better
give him a hand.

18:21.930 --> 18:26.430
KVN, you're going to have
to save the Galaxy 1

18:26.470 --> 18:27.600
someday.

18:27.640 --> 18:29.970
Inside of you
now is the answer.

18:31.770 --> 18:35.110
Hey, Mooncake.
My name is Nightfall.

18:35.140 --> 18:38.010
Don't let Gary die
because of you.

18:42.280 --> 18:44.150
Gary: H.U.E.!
Come in, H.U.E.!

18:44.190 --> 18:46.020
H.U.E.:
Arrr-- yes, Gary?

18:46.050 --> 18:47.760
What the crap,
H.U.E.?!

18:47.790 --> 18:49.290
I've been calling you.

18:49.320 --> 18:51.760
We need you to
scoop us up A.S.A.P.P.!

18:51.790 --> 18:54.360
On my way, Gary.

18:59.830 --> 19:03.270
He-e-e-ey, Gary,
your arm is gone.

19:03.310 --> 19:05.170
Oh, my gosh.
Is it? Really?

19:05.210 --> 19:06.440
I know my arm is gone,

19:06.470 --> 19:08.010
you decaying pile
of fecal matter!

19:08.040 --> 19:09.810
Now get this thing
out of my head, H.U.E.

19:09.840 --> 19:12.110
H.U.E.: Oh. It was never going
to explode, Gary.

19:12.150 --> 19:14.120
That's just
my sense of humor.

19:14.150 --> 19:16.620
You make one joke
in five years,

19:16.650 --> 19:18.790
and that
is the one you tell?

19:18.820 --> 19:22.790
Timing...is everything, Gary.

19:22.820 --> 19:24.990
Hmm.

19:25.030 --> 19:26.130
Whoo.

19:26.160 --> 19:27.730
[ Clank! ]

19:27.760 --> 19:29.730
My arm! My arm!

19:29.760 --> 19:31.470
Interesting.

19:31.500 --> 19:34.870
We can surgically implant
an animatronic arm on you.

19:34.900 --> 19:37.040
Gary, while you were
gone, an intruder --

19:37.070 --> 19:38.740
Shut your face hole, KVN.
Didn't you just hear the news?

19:38.770 --> 19:40.380
I'm getting a robot arm.

19:40.410 --> 19:43.250
But someone will need to
perform the procedure, Gary.

19:43.280 --> 19:45.910
Avocato: I'll do it.

19:49.020 --> 19:51.190
You?

19:51.220 --> 19:54.390
Create temporary
arterial shunt.

19:54.420 --> 19:57.860
I thought we were gonna be
like super friends, man.

19:57.890 --> 20:00.400
I've had one mission for
the past three years, Gary,

20:00.430 --> 20:02.260
and that is
to find my son.

20:02.300 --> 20:05.100
You should have told me.
We did the clasp of friends.

20:05.130 --> 20:07.100
I would have straight-up
helped you get your son back.

20:07.130 --> 20:09.670
What? Why?
You barely know me.

20:09.700 --> 20:12.240
Yo, we played nine hours
of cards together.

20:12.270 --> 20:15.280
That might not mean something
to you, but it did to me.

20:15.310 --> 20:16.940
Expose bone for plating.

20:16.980 --> 20:18.410
Friends help each other
through thick

20:18.450 --> 20:20.950
and thin and thinner
and nothing.

20:20.980 --> 20:22.620
I have nothing
to give in return.

20:22.650 --> 20:25.450
Yeah, you do, yo.
Your friendship, yo.

20:25.490 --> 20:26.850
I've been stuck here
for so long

20:26.890 --> 20:28.190
with just
freakin' robots.

20:28.220 --> 20:31.530
Look robot, robot, robot,
robot, robot, robot!

20:31.560 --> 20:32.560
Freakin' robot.

20:32.590 --> 20:34.060
That's the refrigerator,
Gary.

20:34.100 --> 20:35.960
Really? Because
I've had some serious,

20:36.000 --> 20:37.600
dark conversations
with that thing.

20:37.630 --> 20:40.740
I knows
everything about me.

20:40.770 --> 20:43.870
Keep your mouth shut,
you lying robot!

20:43.910 --> 20:47.680
Micro-vascular transplant
coverage complete.

20:52.010 --> 20:54.750
It's an unconventional way
to start a friendship, but --

20:54.780 --> 20:55.980
Hmm?
-Shh!

20:56.020 --> 20:59.820
No words.
Only clasps.

21:01.790 --> 21:03.390
Bro, you being real
this time?

21:03.430 --> 21:04.760
As real as it gets,
baby.

21:04.790 --> 21:07.460
Then I promise you,
we will get your son back.

21:07.500 --> 21:08.730
And keep Mooncake safe.

21:08.760 --> 21:10.100
And murder
that guy's face off.

21:10.130 --> 21:11.570
I don't think
that's a great idea.

21:11.600 --> 21:13.970
Real raw friendship
mode engaged.

21:14.000 --> 21:16.400
Ooh!

21:16.440 --> 21:26.280
♪♪

21:26.310 --> 21:34.260
♪♪

21:34.290 --> 21:40.060
Where you're going,
your father will never find you.
